# 2. Show patients 11-20 using OFFSET
patients_df.orderBy('patient_id').limit(10).offset(10).show()

# why ouptput is empty?

"""
The output is empty because of the order of the limit() and offset() operations. 
When you use patients_df.orderBy('patient_id').limit(10).offset(10), 
Spark first takes the first 10 patients after ordering (limit(10)). 
Then, it tries to skip 10 patients from that already limited set of 10 patients (offset(10)), 
which results in an empty selection. 
To get patients 11-20, you should apply the offset() first to skip the initial 10 patients, 
and then apply limit() to take the next 10 patients from the remaining dataset. 

"""

